A stall of impossible goods squats on the dry hump of the bog, tended by something that is mostly hat and grin.
"Pollen-Factor Dree Honeythief, licensed by nobody, trusted by fewer. Step closer, climber, the merchandise bites less when it likes you."
He holds up a jar that is, unmistakably, purring. "This one purrs. That's not a defect, climber, that's value."
"Everything here is cursed, yes. A curse is only a feature the previous owner didn't read the manual for."
[You smell honey, ozone, and the specific guilt of about to buy something.]
"No refunds, no resurrections, no questions I'll answer honestly. The marsh keeps a ledger — I keep the better one."
